NAME
    lua - execute Lua 5.5 source code

SYNOPSIS
    lua [-e CODE | FILE | -] [ARG...]
    lua --version

DESCRIPTION
    Runs Lua 5.5.1 source from an inline -e argument, a read-only filesystem
    file, or standard input. Remaining arguments are available in the global
    arg table, starting at arg[1]. With no source argument, reads standard
    input.

    The base, coroutine, table, string, math, and utf8 libraries are present.
    A capability-aware os shim provides clock, difftime, and exit. The other
    standard os functions remain present as extension points and raise a clear
    "unavailable in TROE" error when called. package, io, debug, dynamic
    modules, environment access, and binary bytecode are intentionally
    unavailable. The initial script file is read through the declared
    filesystem capability.

    os.clock returns monotonic seconds elapsed since this Lua invocation with
    millisecond resolution. It measures elapsed time rather than process CPU
    time. os.exit terminates the Lua application with an optional unsigned
    32-bit command status and cannot be caught with pcall. Its second argument
    follows Lua semantics: false (the default) skips Lua-state closing, while
    true closes the state and runs its closing work before termination. TROE
    reclaims the application heap after either form.

    Lua uses a bounded 8 MiB TLSF heap and periodically yields to the KEX
    scheduler. Exhausting the heap raises a normal protected Lua memory error;
    it cannot grow memory or access ambient host resources.

EXAMPLES
    Working example programs are shipped as architecture-independent data:

        lua /share/lua/examples/strings.lua
        lua /share/lua/examples/math.lua
        lua /share/lua/examples/tables-coroutines.lua

    Read them with cat, copy one to /tmp, and adapt it there. The immutable
    originals remain available in the recovery root.
